# A named Structure whose body is one statement, a call with named actuals.
# The reader of declarations passes through a Frame that holds a single Frame,
# and stops at a call; that makes the call no declaration and leaves the
# Structure what it is: a definition whose body runs the call. Solo runs twice
# from the root: f prints its actuals by their formals. A Structure that holds
# one more statement beside the call (Pair) is the neighbour with two fields.
# Entry 7.
fn: f (int: a; int: b) int
    c.printf: "f %d %d\n" a b
return: a - b

Solo:
    f(b: 2; a: 9)
return

Pair:
    int: kept 0
    kept: f(b: 3; a: 8)
return

Solo
Pair
Solo
int: ok 0
if: Pair\kept = 5
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
